# Tier-2 Publish Plane

The editor exposes scenes to the supplier-app (Tier-2) and multi-platform runtime (Tier-3) through a single pure function — `derivePublishedSurface({ nodes, edges }) → PublishedPipeline | { errors }`, exported from `@effects/runtime`. Framework-agnostic (no React, no MUI, no @xyflow/react). Takes a **flat resolved graph** instead of `PageState[]` — editor-side concepts (pages, clones) stay in `apps/editor` via `apps/editor/src/components/node-editor/publish-from-pages.ts → deriveFromPages(pages)` (runs `resolveSceneForEngine` first, then calls into the runtime API). Tier-3 runtimes consume published JSON directly and never see the editor wrapper.

